Analysis: Which columns have no impact on retention?
The following columns appear to have no significant impact on retention:
 - businessTravel
 - DailyRate
 - department
 - DistanceFromHome
 - Education
 - educationField
 - EmployeeCount
 - EmployeeNumber
 - EnvironmentSatisfaction
 - gender
 - HourlyRate
 - JobInvolvement
 - JobSatisfaction
 - maritalStatus
 - MonthlyRate
 - over18
 - overTime
 - PercentSalaryHike
 - PerformanceRating
 - RelationshipSatisfaction
 - StandardHours
 - StockOptionLevel
 - TrainingTimesLastYear
 - WorkLifeBalance

These columns could potentially be removed to simplify data collection.
----------------------------------------
Strategy: We compared the distributions of the best and worst 25% of
employees. Columns where these distributions are statistically
indistinguishable (using cliffs and ks tests) are flagged as irrelevant.

